NOTE, appended 2026-09-16 after reading this log
------------------------------------------------
There is deliberately NO `.rc` file beside this log. The wrapper that produced it ended in
`| tail -6`, so the `echo $?` after it recorded tail's exit code — 0 — for a run that reported
five failures. The file existed, said 0, and was wrong, which is worse than an absent verdict:
the whole point of writing an rc down is that a later reader trusts it without re-reading the log.
It has been deleted rather than corrected, because pytest's own exit code for THIS run was never
captured and inventing 1 would be stating an unmeasured value.

What this log is good for is the failure NAMES above. The verdict lives in
`gates-20260916-step5-rerun.log`, whose rc was captured directly from pytest with no pipe in the
way: rc 1, 3 failed / 587 passed / 7 skipped, and those three are the `claims/tests` members of
the four standing reds in FUTURE-WORK.md item 37. The fifth red visible above — `video/tests`
absent from verify_phase0.sh — was fixed in the same round.
